# Kana keeps all server-side state (password hash, JWT secret, activity DB)
# in SQLite/files under ONE data root resolved by lib/server/data-dir.ts
# (KANA_DATA_DIR → XDG → ~/.local/share/kana). No secrets belong here.
#
# Access password: fresh installs bootstrap with a well-known default
# ("123456") stored ONLY as a bcrypt hash in appstate.db. Change it from the
# UI (Settings → Security) on first login; the login page and
# /api/auth/status surface usingDefaultPassword until you do.
#
# Sessions are stateless HS256 JWT cookies signed with <data dir>/jwt-secret
# (override with KANA_JWT_SECRET).

# Optional explicit data directory (defaults to ~/.local/share/kana).
# KANA_DATA_DIR=/var/lib/kana

# Shared secret for reverse-proxy trust. When set, local-only routes accept
# requests presenting X-Kana-Trusted-Proxy: <value>; when unset the header is
# ignored and only direct-loopback Host/Origin evidence is trusted.
# KANA_TRUSTED_PROXY_SECRET=

# Override the auto-generated session signing secret (64 hex chars).
# KANA_JWT_SECRET=
